From 5b687d75222b48cb1921811bcd9ce519efbcd441 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:32:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ga2: texture regions, button prompts, cheat menu, per-game
 skybox

- gs_texpacks: textures are identified, dumped and replaced per sampled
  region (paraLLEl-GS replacements_cover_rect), since the games declare
  textures larger than their art; dumps are named <hash>_<w>x<h>.png and
  skip the 64-pixel frame-copy strips.
- Button prompts: textures listed in buttons/map.json get the port's own
  icons for the detected input device (Xbox-style pads, keyboard, VR;
  PlayStation pads keep the games' icons) composited at 4x; GA2_BUTTONS
  fixes a style.
- Cheat menu (F1 or L3+R3): skip the running battle with the best result,
  invincibility, infinite energy/spirit, one-hit kills, no time limit; the
  game gets no input while it is open. Hooks live with the game glue.
- GA2_SKYBOX may name a folder with one panorama per program.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
